rtificate authentication\nDescription: Use the SAP Cloud Identity service to manage certificates and authenticate the subscriber applications that share events with SAP Cloud Application Event Hub. See Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-09\nValid as Of: 2024-09-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2322 ---\nComponent: SAPUI5\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: SAPUI5 Distribution 1.128\nDescription: SAPUI5 version 1.128 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. It’s up to the services to determine when they start using the new version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-05\nValid as Of: 2024-09-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2323 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: General Availability of Events\nDescription: You can now create an Events project by using all the available events in the SAP Business Accelerator Hub or by uploading your own specification file. After you create and release the Events project, it can be used in your processes and automations, working as an event trigger to start the process.  See Use Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-04\nValid as Of: 2024-09-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2324 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-03\nValid as Of: 2024-09-03\nVersion: 26612\n\n--- Record 2325 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription: You can duplicate pages in the page preview header.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-03\nValid as Of: 2024-09-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2326 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Region\nDescription: SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery can now also be consumed in the Brazil (São Paulo) region. See Regional Availability.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-02\nValid as Of: 2024-09-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2327 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from OpenAI are supported via Azure.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-02\nValid as Of: 2024-09-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2328 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Image as input is supported for selected models.  For more information, see Chat and Prompt Experimentation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-02\nValid as Of: 2024-09-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2329 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from OpenAI are supported via Azure.  For more information, see Models and Scenarios in the Generative AI Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-02\nValid as Of: 2024-09-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2330 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhanced Error Messages and Extended Export API Functionality \nDescription: We made the following improvements:    Enhanced error messages in the SAP Task Center Administration app for easier troubleshooting.      Extended Export API to include task definitions in the exported file.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-02\nValid as Of: 2024-09-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2801 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Store - New Content Packages\nDescription: A set of 7 content packages (6 business, 1 learning) were added to the Store in April and May 2024.      Learning Content:  HR position planning  SAP S/4HANA Cloud, Public Edition:  Mass Creation Of Business Solution Orders(6O3)  Mass Creation Of Business Solution Orders(6O3)  Mass Maintenance of Enterprise Projects(4JA)    SAP Complaint Handling:  Entry Validation Rules for SAP Complaint Handling  SAP Integrated Business Planning for Supply Chain:  Process Step Start Approval for SAP IBP for Supply Chain  SAP Sustainability Control Tower:  SAP Sustainability Control Tower – Data Collection Forms  Updates and Bug Fixes:  Purchase Requisition Header Approval and Release  Journal Entry Posting Approval  Process Order Confirmation (BAPI)  Creation of Goods Receipt (BAPI)  Creation of Business Partner (BAPI)  Creation of Sales Order (BAPI)  Creation of Purchase Requisition (BAPI)  Cost Center Change Multiple (BAPI)    Deprecated Packages:  [DEPRECATED] Document Centric Approval Process  Mass creation of Business Solution Orders (6O3)      \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-07\nValid as Of: 2024-06-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2802 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   Company MLTR now supports import of ABAP object lists  \nDescription:   You can now import your translations from an ABAP object list into your company MLTR in addition to importing XLIFF 1.2 files.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Restricted Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-07\nValid as Of: 2024-06-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2803 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   Translation of ABAP short text objects with source languages other than English (e.g. German)  \nDescription:   You can now use the ABAP integration to translate ABAP short texts in source languages other than English, such as for example German.   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Restricted Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-07\nValid as Of: 2024-06-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2804 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhancements to Maintain Promotions app\nDescription: The following changes are now available in the Maintain Promotions app:      Renaming of the Verify button to Check Master Data.      Renaming of the Invalidate button to Cancel.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2805 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extension Point for Customized Promotion Master Data Validations\nDescription: You can now add custom logic to validate promotion master data.  With the implementation of this extension, you can run your specific promotion master data checks. The extension can be called by using the new Validate button in the Maintain Promotions app.  For more information, see Getting Started with Extensibility for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing and Customized Promotion Master Data Validation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2806 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Attributes for Identifying Last Calculation-Relevant Changes in Regular Prices and Promotions\nDescription: You can now use the new attribute lastCalcRelevantChange that is available for both regular prices and promotions. With this attribute that represents a timestamp, you can:     search and select all regular prices with calculation-relevant changes after a specific point in time,       search and select promotions with calculation-relevant changes after a specific point in time.      In the case of regular prices, the attribute is updated when a calculation-relevant change is made using the Data Upload service.  In the case of promotions, the attribute is updated when a calculation-relevant change is made using the Data Upload service or on the Maintain Promotions UI.  For more information about the use cases and examples, see Data Access.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2807 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Product Experience (PX) Survey for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nDescription: You can now provide feedback for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing in real-time right from your SAP Fiori Launchpad.  With Product Experience (PX) survey, you can either initiate the feedback process from your end using the icon provided or utilize the application-triggered prompts at regular intervals.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2808 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer", " from your SAP Fiori Launchpad.  With Product Experience (PX) survey, you can either initiate the feedback process from your end using the icon provided or utilize the application-triggered prompts at regular intervals.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General