ctory of SAP Cloud Identity Services.   Currently, it is supported for SAP Advanced Financial Closing only.  See List of Properties →ips.application.id.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-17\nVersion: 26387\n\n--- Record 2589 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity", " distinguish groups provisioned from various source systems to the Identity Directory of SAP Cloud Identity Services.   Currently, it is supported for SAP Advanced Financial Closing only.  See List of Properties →ips.application.id.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-17\nVersion: 26387\n\n--- Record 2589 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Local Identity Directory - group mapping\nDescription: The default transformations of Local Identity Directory provisioning systems are extended to support the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:Group schema, which contains the applicationId, type and supportedOperationsgroup attributes.  The applicationId allows Identity Provisioning to replicate application-specific groups to the Identity Directory.  See:  Groups  Local Identity Directory (Source)  Local Identity Directory (Target)  Local Identity Directory (Proxy)    List of Properties →ips.application.id      \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-17\nVersion: 26387\n\n--- Record 2590 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Procurement Data Warehouse connector\nDescription: Identity Provisioning supports the Procurement Data Warehouse connector. You can configure it as source, target, and proxy system for your provisioning scenarios. See:    Procurement Data Warehouse (Source)      Procurement Data Warehouse (Target)      Procurement Data Warehouse (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-17\nVersion: 26387\n\n", "--- Record 2141 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: 26753\n\n--- Record 2142 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Regions\nDescription: SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery can now also be consumed in the US Central (IA) and Asia Pacific (Singapore) regions. See Regional Availability.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2143 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Administrator's Guide\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Introducing the SAP BTP Administrator's Guide\nDescription: We’ve improved the documentation structure to more effectively meet the needs of our users:   What was formerly known as “Best Practices for SAP BTP” is now targeted towards administrative tasks and best practices, providing a more streamlined resource for administrators. It has therefore been renamed to SAP BTP Administrator's Guide.  All our recommendations about developing applications, some of which used to be part of the Best Practices as well, have been consolidated in the SAP BTP Developer’s Guide.   This restructuring aims to ensure that both developers and administrators can easily find relevant and specialized guidance.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2144 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2024.21\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data modeling, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2024.21. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2145 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changes to the SAP Document AI Basic UI\nDescription: We’ve made a number of enhancements to the SAP Document AI basic UI.       When you upload a document and choose it on the Documents screen, you now see the extraction results for header fields and line items alongside the document preview, without first having to click Extraction Results.      In the extraction results, you can now use the filters at the top of the Edit pane to set which extraction confidence ranges to display. You can select either a single range or all of them.      When using the Template feature, you can now edit and confirm extraction results for the associated document by choosing it on the details page for the template you've created.      Also on the Template details page, you can now set an extraction method for individual fields or for all fields your template. The available methods are Template and AI.      See View and Edit Extraction Results, Add Documents and Activate/Deactivate Template, and Add Template.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2146 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Factur-X and ZUGFeRD Standards - Support for Version 2.3\nDescription: SAP Document AI now supports the version 2.3 of e-invoice document files in Factur-X and ZUGFeRD standards.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2147 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Instant Learning for Information Extraction Using Generative AI (Premium Edition)\nDescription: SAP Document AI now allows you to enhance extraction with generative AI by using your edited extraction results to enrich the prompt to large language models (LLMs) with user feedback.  If you use an appropriately configured schema, SAP Document AI learns from your feedback as soon you commit documents with edited extraction results. As a result, information extraction is improved for relevant fields in all subsequent documents.  To use this feature, you must first activate it using the configuration key enableInstantLearning.  See Instant Learning (Premium Edition) and Configuration Keys.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-22\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2148 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New List of Values Data Type for Schemas (Premium Edition)\nDescription: With SAP Document AI you can now use the data type list of values to extract header or line item fields with the setup type auto.  The new data type allows you to define multiple values for fields. For example, if your company handles three different types of invoice, you can define these as list values. As a result, only these values are extracted for Invoice Type fields in your documents. ", " Foundry\nTitle: New List of Values Data Type for Schemas (Premium Edition)\nDescription: With SAP Document AI you can now use the data type list of values to extract header or line item fields with the setup type auto.  The new data type allows you to define multiple values for fields. For example, if your company handles three different types of invoice, you can define these as list values. As a result, only these values are extracted for Invoice Type fields in your documents.  See List of Values Data Type (Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2149 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Schema Import and Schema Export Endpoints\nDescription: You can now import and export schemas using the following new Schema API endpoints:    Import Schema      Export Schema    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2150 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Collecting Data and Performance Metrics\nDescription: Performance and usage metrics of applications deployed on SAP BTP can be measured using the Front-End Statistical Records (FESR) tool. The results of these metrics, called performance artifacts, are collected, and transferred to SAP Cloud ALM (CALM) service that sends the data to cloud reporting.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-30\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: 2409B\n\n", "--- Record 2411 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Deprecated Business Catalog for Analytical Queries\nDescription: The business catalog SAP_A4C_BC_DEV_PC used for the preview of analytical queries will be removed. Please use its successor BC SAP_A4C_BC_DEV_DAT_PRV_PC instead. Both business catalogs require the Developer business role.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2412 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Business Configurations: Recreation of Variants Needed\nDescription: You need to recreate variants for the list report of the Fiori app Custom Business Configurations due to a change in the persistence key.  For more information, see SAP note: 3486327 .\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2413 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ABAP Debugger: Variables with Hidden Values\nDescription: In the ABAP Debugger, the variable values with a type that is based on the domains XUBCODE, RSECDATA or DISPLAY_PROTECTED_STRING/DISPLAY_PROTECTED_XSTRING, are now hidden in the Variables view and in the ABAP Internal Table (Debugger) view. The values, for example of passwords or other sensitive data, will then be displayed as ******** or DEADDA7A.  See Symbols with Hidden Content.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2414 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Assigning Fiori Space Templates to Business Role Templates\nDescription: You can now assign Fiori Space templates to business role templates. When a business role is created from a business role template, the related Fiori Spaces are assigned.  See Working with Business Role Template Launchpad Space Template Assignments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2415 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ATC Checks now Support List of Classic APIs\nDescription: Should released APIs for ABAP Cloud be missing, the ABAP Extensibility Guide recommends creating a custom API wrapper. The ATC checks “Usage of Released APIs” and “Usage of Released APIs (Cloudification Repository)”, which are classic APIs that are recommended to be used in a wrapper, were adjusted. If you're using a SAP BTP ABAP environment system as your central ATC check system, no ATC error is shown in case an API classified as classic is used in custom code. Instead, you’ll only receive a warning.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2416 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Browser for Cloudification Repository Content\nDescription: You can now browse through the content of the Cloudification Repository on GitHub.  See Cloudification Repository Viewer.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2417 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Communication Targets for HTTP Outbound Communication\nDescription: The usage of the new application destinations via outbound services of type communication target is recommended when developing a new application with HTTP outbound communication. This enables developers to define and control which applications can use a particular application destination.  See Working with Communication Targets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2418 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating API Package Assignments\nDescription: You can now assign APIs to API packages. An API package assignment is a container that defines the assignment between the API package and the corresponding API object.  See Working with API Package Assignments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2419 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating API Packages\nDescription: You can now create API packages. An API package is a container that can hold different types of APIs.  See", " General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2419 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating API Packages\nDescription: You can now create API packages. An API package is a container that can hold different types of APIs.  See Working with API Packages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2420 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Background Processing Contexts\nDescription: You can now create your own background processing contexts. A background processing context allows asynchronous processing.  See Working with Background Queue Contexts.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embed